  "query_preview": "..\n(Saturday night through Thursday)\nIssued at 317 AM EDT Fri Oct 23 2026\n\nAs has been the case for quite some time, the forecast through the \nend of next week remains on the quiet side. Precipitation chances \nwill remain nil as high pressure will dominate and indications of \nmore substantial opportunities for rain staying just beyond the end of \nthe current forecast period.\n\nIn the meantime, a CAD wedge will be the dominant feature through \nthe weekend while the surface high will migrate southward into early \nnext week. Thus, cooler temperatures early in the week will \ngradually modify and warm from mid-to-late week. All this means is \nearly week temperatures will creep from near to slightly below \nnormal to a few degrees above normal. Meanwhile, the upper pattern \nbecomes much less amplified and begins to transition to a more \nsouthwesterly flow by the end of the week, potentially leading into \na wetter pattern headed into November.",
